<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> Chronicle is a collection of annals in Old English recording the history of the English from the Roman period to the twelfth century. First compiled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> in the late ninth century, during the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, it was copied and continued in several monasteries, and the last entries in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peterborough">Peterborough</a> version reach 1154. It is the main narrative source for Wessex and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle.jpg" alt="Anglo-Saxon Chronicle" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographed by Geogre, original author, monastic scribes in Peterborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peterborough.Chronicle.firstpage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
